Definition

A group of people that share a characteristic (i.e. race, class, gender, age) that is legally protected from discrimination originated from the characteristic.

Brief History

Civil Rights Act of 1964

Title VII of this landmark law prohibited discrimination in employment based on race, color, religion, sex, or national origin. It also established the Equal Employment Opportunity Commission (EEOC) to enforce these protections.";}s:8:"relation";a:2:{s:10:"references";a:4:{s:33:"sidebar:glossary:disparate_impact";b:0;s:36:"sidebar:glossary:disparate_treatment";b:0;s:35:"sidebar:glossary:protected_activity";b:0;s:29:"sidebar:categories:compliance";b:1;}s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}s:8:"internal";a:2:{s:5:"cache";b:1;s:3:"toc";b:1;}s:11:"contributor";a:1:{s:5:"admin";s:11:"Aditya Seth";}}s:10:"persistent";a:5:{s:4:"date";a:2:{s:7:"created";i:1743109863;s:8:"modified";i:1743110050;}s:7:"creator";s:11:"Aditya Seth";s:4:"user";s:5:"admin";s:11:"last_change";a:9:{s:4:"date";i:1743110050;s:2:"ip";s:14:"73.235.164.232";s:4:"type";s:1:"E";s:2:"id";s:45:"sidebar:categories:compliance:protected_class";s:4:"user";s:5:"admin";s:3:"sum";s:0:"";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";s:10:"sizechange";i:238;s:4:"mode";s:4:"page";}s:11:"contributor";a:1:{s:5:"admin";s:11:"Aditya Seth";}}}